# Root environment reference — INDEX ONLY, not read by any tool.
#
# Scaffold-ETH 2 reads environment variables per-package, not from the repo root:
#   packages/foundry/.env        — contracts, deploy, verification (copied
#                                   automatically from packages/foundry/.env.example
#                                   on `yarn install`)
#   packages/nextjs/.env.local   — frontend (copy packages/nextjs/.env.example
#                                   yourself: `cp packages/nextjs/.env.example
#                                   packages/nextjs/.env.local`)
#
# This file exists so "what secrets does this project need" has one answer you
# can read without opening both packages. Edit the real files above, not this one.
#
# Full required-vs-optional matrix per environment (local/testnet/production):
# docs/development.md

# ============================================================================
# SECRETS (packages/foundry/.env — never commit, never print, never share)
# ============================================================================
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY        — empty for local Anvil; generated via `yarn generate`
#                                for testnet/production. NEVER a mainnet key locally.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY           — verify on Ethereum/Optimism/Arbitrum (Etherscan v2)
# BASESCAN_API_KEY            — verify on Base / Base Sepolia (default L2 target)
# POLYGONSCAN_API_KEY         — verify on Polygon / Polygon Amoy

# ============================================================================
# PUBLIC (packages/foundry/.env)
# ============================================================================
# ALCHEMY_API_KEY              — only for mainnet/arbitrum/optimism/polygon RPCs;
#                                 not needed for the hackathon's default path
# PRODUCTION_RPC_URL            — required only for `yarn deploy --network production`
# LOCALHOST_KEYSTORE_ACCOUNT    — defaults to "scaffold-eth-default" (Anvil account #9)

# ============================================================================
# PUBLIC (packages/nextjs/.env.local — NEXT_PUBLIC_* is bundled client-side)
# ============================================================================
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY          — only for chains without a free public RPC
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID — get your own before a public demo
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD                — "true" only for the static export build
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR        — emergency-only; never on by default

# ============================================================================
# CI / DEPLOYMENT SECRETS (GitHub Actions — Settings → Secrets and variables)
# ============================================================================
# Same DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY / *_API_KEY secrets as above, plus, only if you wire
# up Vercel deploys through GitHub Actions instead of Vercel's own Git integration:
# VERCEL_TOKEN, VERCEL_ORG_ID, VERCEL_PROJECT_ID
✓ Vercel configured on 2026-09-22
